Function Dot_Product(X1, X2: Array[P]; P:Index )
Title: Dot Product
Description: Finds the dot product (or inner product) of vectors X1 and X2. Both vectors are indexed by P, which is the vector of orthogonal principal directions, P:=['i', 'j' ,..., 'k'].~
~
If X1['i', 'j', 'k'] := (a, b, c) and X2['i', 'j', 'k'] := (d, e, f), then X1 <o> X2 gives a scalar value that is the sum of the pairwise products of the vectors.~
X1 <*> X2 = a*d + b*e + c*f
Definition: Sum(X1 * X2, P)
